    "rendered": "<div class=\"xyz-content\"><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"shell pt-6\"> <ol class=\"m-0 flex list-none flex-wrap items-center gap-2 p-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\"> <li class=\"flex items-center gap-2\">  <a href=\"/\" class=\"no-underline hover:underline\"> Home </a> </li><li class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"> <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-rule\"> / </span> <span aria-current=\"page\">FAQ</span> </li> </ol> </nav> <div class=\"shell pt-6\"> <p class=\"band-eyebrow\">Common questions</p> <h1 class=\"text-3xl sm:text-4xl\">Questions</h1> <p class=\"mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[1.0625rem]\"> If yours is not here, <a href=\"/contact/\">ask us</a> — and we will add it. </p> </div> <section class=\"shell mt-20\" aria-labelledby=\"the-calculators-heading\"> <h2 id=\"the-calculators-heading\" class=\"text-2xl\">The calculators</h2> <dl class=\"mt-6 border-t border-rule\"> <div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Are the calculators really free?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Yes. No email, no account, no limit on how many times you use them. We charge for preparing and lodging a return, not for arithmetic.</dd> </div><div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">How accurate are they?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">The tax engine is unit tested against the ATO published tables at every bracket boundary, and for every <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$1,000</span> step from <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$0</span> to <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$500,000</span> across three financial years. Where a figure is provisional because the ATO has not yet indexed it, the calculator says so. They are still estimates: a real assessment also uses the data the ATO holds about you.</dd> </div><div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Which financial year should I pick?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">The year the income was earned. A return being lodged now covers the year ended 30 June 2026, which is 2025-26. Pick 2026-27 if you are working out take-home pay for the year you are in.</dd> </div><div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Can I share a calculation with someone?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Yes. Every calculator writes your figures into the address bar, so copying the URL shares exactly what you were looking at. Nothing identifying is included.</dd> </div> </dl> </section><section class=\"shell mt-20\" aria-labelledby=\"lodging-with-us-heading\"> <h2 id=\"lodging-with-us-heading\" class=\"text-2xl\">Lodging with us</h2> <dl class=\"mt-6 border-t border-rule\"> <div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">What does it cost?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Individual returns are <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$99,</span> investments <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$179,</span> sole traders <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$299</span>. Fixed, quoted before we start, and deductible next year. Full pricing is published on the pricing page.</dd> </div><div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">How long does it take?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">The intake form takes about ten minutes. We usually have a draft return back to you within two business days, and the ATO typically assesses an electronically lodged return within two weeks.</dd> </div><div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Can the fee come out of my refund?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Yes, for individual returns, and it costs <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$44</span>. The refund goes to our trust account, we deduct the fee and forward the balance, usually within a business day. Pay the fee up front instead and the <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$44</span> does not apply.</dd> </div><div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Do you handle late or unlodged returns?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Regularly. If you have several years outstanding we can put them on a lodgement program and work through them in order. The usual outcome is money back rather than a bill, and the ATO treats voluntary catch-up very differently from being chased.</dd> </div> </dl> </section><section class=\"shell mt-20\" aria-labelledby=\"privacy-and-security-heading\"> <h2 id=\"privacy-and-security-heading\" class=\"text-2xl\">Privacy and security</h2> <dl class=\"mt-6 border-t border-rule\"> <div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Do you ask for my tax file number?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Never on this website, including the intake form. TFNs are subject to the Privacy (Tax File Number) Rule 2015. We collect yours through a secure channel once an accountant is working on your return.</dd> </div><div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">What do the calculators send to your servers?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Nothing. Every calculation runs in your browser. We use privacy-focused analytics that records that a calculator was used, never the figures you typed.</dd> </div><div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Why do I have to verify my identity for a simple tax return?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Because a tax return is exactly what identity thieves lodge. Every client — every return, every service — completes a three-minute electronic ID check on their phone before we start: a licence or passport, a selfie, and a match against government records. It is included in the fee, the TPB requires tax agents to verify every client, and it keeps your refund out of someone else&#8217;s account. <a href=\"/identity-verification/\">How the check works</a>.</dd> </div><div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\"> <dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Are you actually registered?</dt> <dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Yes — tax agent number 26233684. Anyone charging a fee to prepare or lodge a return must be registered with the Tax Practitioners Board, and the register is free to search. Check us, and check anyone else you are considering.</dd> </div> </dl> </section><section class=\"cta-dark\"> <div class=\"cta-grid\"> <div> <p class=\"band-eyebrow\">Ready to lodge it?</p> <h2>A registered agent prepares it, checks it, and lodges it.</h2> <p>Most refunds land within two weeks of assessment. The fee is fixed and quoted before we start — nothing is charged until you approve the finished return.</p> <div class=\"cta-actions\"> <a href=\"https://brsadvisory.myassembly.com/login?step=signUp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"btn\">Start your return</a> <a href=\"/services/pricing/\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\">See pricing</a> </div> </div> <div class=\"cta-spec\"> <div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Individual returns from</span><b>$99</b></div> <div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Registered tax agent</span><b>26233684</b></div> <div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Fixed fee, quoted up front</span><i>included</i></div> <div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Identity check, every client</span><i>included</i></div> <div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Fee taken from your refund</span><b>$44</b></div> </div> </div> </section></div>\n<div hidden class=\"xyz-schema\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"@id\":\"https://superblyladyec52fb18e8-stxdq.wpcomstaging.com/faq/#faq\",\"url\":\"https://superblyladyec52fb18e8-stxdq.wpcomstaging.com/faq/\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Are the calculators really free?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. No email, no account, no limit on how many times you use them. We charge for preparing and lodging a return, not for arithmetic.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How accurate are they?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The tax engine is unit tested against the ATO published tables at every bracket boundary, and for every $1,000 step from $0 to $500,000 across three financial years. Where a figure is provisional because the ATO has not yet indexed it, the calculator says so. They are still estimates: a real assessment also uses the data the ATO holds about you.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which financial year should I pick?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The year the income was earned. A return being lodged now covers the year ended 30 June 2026, which is 2025-26. Pick 2026-27 if you are working out take-home pay for the year you are in.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I share a calculation with someone?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. Every calculator writes your figures into the address bar, so copying the URL shares exactly what you were looking at. Nothing identifying is included.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What does it cost?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Individual returns are $99, investments $179, sole traders $299 . Fixed, quoted before we start, and deductible next year. Full pricing is published on the pricing page.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How long does it take?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The intake form takes about ten minutes. We usually have a draft return back to you within two business days, and the ATO typically assesses an electronically lodged return within two weeks.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can the fee come out of my refund?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, for individual returns, and it costs $44 . The refund goes to our trust account, we deduct the fee and forward the balance, usually within a business day. Pay the fee up front instead and the $44 does not apply.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do you handle late or unlodged returns?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Regularly. If you have several years outstanding we can put them on a lodgement program and work through them in order. The usual outcome is money back rather than a bill, and the ATO treats voluntary catch-up very differently from being chased.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do you ask for my tax file number?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Never on this website, including the intake form. TFNs are subject to the Privacy (Tax File Number) Rule 2015. We collect yours through a secure channel once an accountant is working on your return.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What do the calculators send to your servers?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Nothing. Every calculation runs in your browser. We use privacy-focused analytics that records that a calculator was used, never the figures you typed.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Why do I have to verify my identity for a simple tax return?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Because a tax return is exactly what identity thieves lodge. Every client — every return, every service — completes a three-minute electronic ID check on their phone before we start: a licence or passport, a selfie, and a match against government records. It is included in the fee, the TPB requires tax agents to verify every client, and it keeps your refund out of someone else’s account. How the check works .\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Are you actually registered?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes — tax agent number 26233684. Anyone charging a fee to prepare or lodge a return must be registered with the Tax Practitioners Board, and the register is free to search. Check us, and check anyone else you are considering.\"}}]}</script></div>\n"
